# photoshowcase.service unit install -- deploy user, root context.
#
# Lets CD install infra/systemd/photoshowcase.service and reload the systemd
# manager on every deploy, instead of a human running `sudo install` +
# `daemon-reload` by hand. See infra/README.md section 4 for what this
# unblocks and task #102 for the history.
#
# BE PLAIN ABOUT WHAT THIS GRANT IS: it is root-equivalent for `deploy`, full
# stop. `deploy` already controls the ExecStart= a root-owned unit runs, and
# `deploy` already holds `systemctl restart photoshowcase.service` (see
# photoshowcase-deploy in this same directory) -- so letting it write this
# one unit file lets it run anything as root on the next restart. The
# literal source/destination paths below bound WHICH file gets written, not
# what a hostile or buggy `deploy` could put in it; they do not shrink the
# blast radius of a compromised or mistaken `deploy`, only of a `deploy` that
# mistypes a path. The actual enforcement boundary is PR review of
# infra/systemd/photoshowcase.service, branch protection on `main`, custody
# of the DEPLOY_SSH_KEY secret, and who may dispatch the Deploy workflow --
# not sudoers narrowness.
#
# NOT a new escalation on this droplet, either: findash-redis-provision (also
# in this directory) already grants `deploy` an equivalent root-equivalent
# pattern -- installing a unit file as root -- plus a redis restart. This
# file is a second instance of a power `deploy` already has on this box, not
# a fresh one. (That existing grant has the /tmp staging flaw this file
# avoids -- see below; it belongs to another service with another owner and
# is tracked separately as task #108 -- do not touch it here.)
#
# Source path is $UNIT_STAGING_DIR (/home/deploy/staging, 0700, created by
# the pipeline under deploy's own 0750-with-empty-group home), not /tmp:
# /tmp is world-writable, and this droplet has other local principals with a
# real /tmp view outside any PrivateTmp sandbox -- the cron backup jobs
# (running as findash, photoshowcase, zyeth; cron does not apply
# PrivateTmp=) and an interactive shell as any of those users. (The
# `findash`/`photoshowcase`/`zyeth` *services themselves* do set
# PrivateTmp=true and were never the exposure -- their cron-run backup
# scripts and any interactive login were.) /home/deploy is 0750 with an
# empty `deploy` group, so only `deploy` and root can even traverse it,
# which is what actually excludes those principals -- not the /tmp sticky
# bit, which only blocks unlink/rename by non-owners, not pre-creating a
# file or symlink they own.
#
# /home/deploy/staging/photoshowcase.service is written by the "Install
# systemd unit" / "Rollback on failure" steps in
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml via a plain (non-sudo) scp as the deploy
# user, so no sudo grant is needed for that half.
#
# /usr/bin/systemctl below is the same binary the sibling *-deploy sudoers
# files reference as /bin/systemctl (/bin is a symlink to /usr/bin on this
# droplet, Ubuntu 24.04 usrmerge). No sibling file references `install` in
# any form; that binary is used here directly, not by analogy.
deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/install -m 0644 -o root -g root /home/deploy/staging/photoshowcase.service /etc/systemd/system/photoshowcase.service
deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl daemon-reload
